@startuml sequence-digitalizer-render-service
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: render on a service is a chained stage: the orchestrator's own
'       prepare step (metadata lookup, the item's text documents, a request
'       file on the shared storage) and then render-service's book job (the
'       media); applying the book renames the media into the IA item layout
'       and writes the rows and the IA XML documents with the same code as
'       the orchestrator's render.finish.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one book, as implemented on the orchestrator
'       side; render-service is proposed (evilflowers-render-service#1).
'       Omitted: pump admission (render is an off-peak stage), reconcile, SSE.
' Source: this repo studio/workers/stages/render.py (prepare, finish),
'         studio/orchestration/{ledger,contract,appliers}.py, studio/config.py
'         (CHAINED_STAGES, DEFAULT_PARTS) (2026-11-16); knowledge#66 and Key-Value
'         (Valkey db 8, 2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Render stage: prepare here, media on render-service (orchestrator side implemented, 2026-11-16)

participant "Orchestrator\n(job ledger)" as orch <<focus>>
participant "OPAC" as opac
queue "Valkey db 8" as redis
participant "render-service\nevilflowers_render.book" as rs <<proposed>>
collections "Shared storage\n{storage_root}" as fs

orch -> orch : formulas applied: plan render/prepare\n(the orchestrator's own job, portal queue)
orch -> opac : metadata lookup (OCR text: ISBN)
orch -> fs : _hocr.html, _djvu.txt, regions.json;\nrender/request-<run>.json + access hOCR
orch -> orch : prepare applied: plan render/book
orch -[$accent_msg()]> redis : <b>send_task evilflowers_render.book</b>\n<b>request (path) · output_dir · outcome · token</b>\n<b>link=job_done · link_error=job_failed</b>
redis -> rs : deliver (off-peak)
rs -> fs : read request: pages, hOCR, metadata,\nformats, regions (EPUB), JP2 leaves
rs -> fs : <id>.pdf (MRC, JPEG) · <id>_archival.pdf (PDF/A-2b, JP2)\n<id>.epub · <id>_jp2.zip; outcome last (size, md5, pdfa_valid)
rs -> redis : link: job_done
redis -[$accent_msg()]> orch : <b>job_done</b>
orch -> fs : check every file (requested, in the attempt, size);\nrename into the item (IA names)
orch -> orch : rows: artifacts, PDF page map, n_pages;\nIA XML (_meta, _scandata, _files) from the rows
orch -> fs : after commit: delete the attempt dir

caption The service writes only media; the IA XML documents come from the rows the orchestrator owns. Nothing is moved\nunless every requested format is there; a failed PDF/A check fails the job.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/sequence-digitalizer-render-service.puml
@enduml
